  "worked_solution": "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {((2t+2)-2)}^{2}+{(2t-4)}^{2}+{(-2\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+(4{t}^{2}-16t+16)+8{t}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}-16t+16 & =16 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}-16t & =0 \\\\ t(t-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+2=2 \\\\ y=2(0)-4=-4 \\\\ z=-2\\sqrt{2}(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(2,-4,0).$\n\n- For $t=1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(1)+2=4 \\\\ y=2(1)-4=-2 \\\\ z=-2\\sqrt{2}(1)=-2\\sqrt{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(4,-2,-2\\sqrt{2}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(2,-4,0)$ and $(4,-2,-2\\sqrt{2}).$",
